1
00:00:16,225 --> 00:00:19,228
<i>Tonight, a</i> 60 Minutes <i>exclusive.</i>

2
00:00:20,062 --> 00:00:24,815
<i>Ten years ago, no one on Earth was aware
we were already under the protection</i>

3
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:27,736
<i>of someone calling himself Green Lantern.</i>

4
00:00:28,362 --> 00:00:31,697
<i>Then, without warning,
he made himself known,</i>

5
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:36,285
<i>dramatically stopping a meteor
from devastating Victoria Falls.</i>

6
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:39,039
<i>Or, at least,
he made himself partially known.</i>

7
00:00:40,332 --> 00:00:45,379
<i>Here now, we bring you the first ever
heart-to-heart with a superhero.</i>

8
00:00:46,505 --> 00:00:47,506
<i>Are you nervous?</i>

9
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:49,382
<i>I don't get nervous.</i>

10
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:51,676
<i>- Part of the job description.
- Of course.</i>

11
00:00:51,677 --> 00:00:53,177
<i>Excited.</i>

12
00:00:53,178 --> 00:00:55,389
<i>In that case, who are you?</i>

13
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:58,475
<i>I'm Hal Jordan.</i>

14
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:00,893
Damn it, Marcus!

15
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:04,314
- You're gonna get us all in trouble.
- Just watch the window!

16
00:01:07,526 --> 00:01:10,862
<i>So, what do you want the world
to know about you?</i>

17
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:13,031
<i>I'm an Air Force veteran.</i>

18
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:15,033
<i>I'm a former test pilot.</i>

19
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:17,077
<i>And really...</i>

20
00:01:21,415 --> 00:01:23,166
<i>just that I'm a regular person.</i>

21
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:24,918
<i>Like you.</i>

22
00:01:25,586 --> 00:01:29,548
<i>Except that you're also
Earth's first Green Lantern.</i>

23
00:01:30,173 --> 00:01:31,300
<i>There is that, too.</i>

24
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:36,179
<i>In many ways, Hal Jordan was born
for the role he would eventually play.</i>

25
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,973
<i>His father was a decorated test pilot</i>

26
00:01:38,974 --> 00:01:42,227
<i>who died tragically in a crash
when Hal was just eight.</i>

27
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:46,272
<i>Hal continued to follow
in his father's footsteps...</i>

28
00:01:46,273 --> 00:01:48,482
Shit, shit, shit! He's home!

29
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:50,985
Damn it! Come on, John, turn the TV off!

30
00:01:50,986 --> 00:01:55,114
<i>Well, I'm the only one here,
but we're like beat cops.</i>

31
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:56,657
<i>- Only each one of us...</i>
- Turn it off!

32
00:01:56,658 --> 00:01:58,075
<i>...has a chunk of the galaxy.</i>

33
00:01:58,076 --> 00:02:00,911
<i>And how are you chosen for this chunk?</i>

34
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:02,455
<i>- Is there a test?</i>
- John!

35
00:02:02,456 --> 00:02:05,334
- Come on, turn the TV off!
<i>- It's only one question.</i>

36
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:08,587
- We're so dead.
<i>- "Are you afraid?"</i>

37
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:11,757
<i>And you said, "No."</i>

38
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:13,508
<i>I did.</i>

39
00:02:14,176 --> 00:02:18,472
<i>Every kid's worst fear is losing a parent.</i>

40
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:21,099
<i>Once that happens...</i>

41
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:26,021
<i>there is nothing to fear anymore.</i>

42
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,835
So you gonna tell me his real name?

43
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:53,090
Hal something.

44
00:02:53,674 --> 00:02:54,675
Hal?

45
00:02:55,217 --> 00:02:56,343
Yes, sir.

46
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:01,431
Outside. Now.

47
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:29,209
Are you afraid?

48
00:03:30,585 --> 00:03:31,712
No, sir!

49
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:01,575
Let's go get a burger.

50
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:24,514
Shit.

51
00:05:04,596 --> 00:05:05,597
I'm late.

52
00:05:07,933 --> 00:05:08,934
Yes, sir.

53
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:11,603
You're not gonna say anything?

54
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:32,122
You sure you're not mad?

55
00:05:32,123 --> 00:05:34,459
- No, sir.
- Me, I'd be pissed off.

56
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:36,919
Disappearing for two weeks,

57
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:40,298
no explanation,
show up hungover, and late.

58
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:43,634
Come on, you gotta be a little angry.

59
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:45,095
No, sir.

60
00:05:46,388 --> 00:05:47,638
Mildly perturbed?

61
00:05:47,639 --> 00:05:49,265
No, sir.

62
00:05:49,266 --> 00:05:51,308
How come it is every time you say "sir,"

63
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:53,227
it sounds more and more like, "Fuck you"?

64
00:05:53,228 --> 00:05:54,813
I have no idea.

65
00:05:55,355 --> 00:05:56,565
Sir.

66
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:01,944
You must be wondering where I was.

67
00:06:01,945 --> 00:06:04,864
- You ever heard of Pharon 4?
- Well, we're in training.

68
00:06:04,865 --> 00:06:06,490
We haven't gone off-planet yet.

69
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:09,034
Yeah, yeah, that's right.
It's a shithole of a planet

70
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:10,661
that was on the verge of civil war.

71
00:06:10,662 --> 00:06:12,830
The point is, if I'm hungover,

72
00:06:12,831 --> 00:06:15,332
it's only because
I was celebrating the new peace.

73
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:16,584
So, how'd you manage it?

74
00:06:16,585 --> 00:06:19,212
A little bit of diplomacy,
a little punching, you know the drill.

75
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:21,422
Actually, I don't, sir. That's the point.

76
00:06:21,423 --> 00:06:23,382
Well, you got all the time in the world.

77
00:06:23,383 --> 00:06:24,592
With all due respect,

78
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:27,012
we've been doing this, what, two months?

79
00:06:28,597 --> 00:06:30,222
And I haven't even worn the ring yet.

80
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:33,767
Don't get hung up on the jewelry, Junior.
You'll wear it when it chooses you.

81
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:36,312
I thought the point was
that the Guardians chose me.

82
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:38,147
- That's all.
- The big blue bosses

83
00:06:38,148 --> 00:06:39,440
may think that you're hot shit,

84
00:06:39,441 --> 00:06:42,234
but you're just a fucking
substitute teacher, Junior.

85
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:44,028
You're not ready to get up
in front of the class

86
00:06:44,029 --> 00:06:45,488
until the ring says you are.

87
00:06:53,997 --> 00:06:54,998
Here.

88
00:06:55,582 --> 00:06:56,833
You wanna take it?

89
00:06:57,584 --> 00:06:59,044
Is that a test?

90
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:04,381
There's a taco stand up the road
about three miles.

91
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:05,675
I'll meet you there.

92
00:07:45,548 --> 00:07:48,175
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Dad, he tried to kill me.

93
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:50,886
We was on our way
to a flying lesson, and he--

94
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:52,805
Jordan just tried to fucking kill me.

95
00:07:52,806 --> 00:07:54,473
<i>He can't kill you.</i>

96
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:55,976
<i>He's just trying to put you on tilt.</i>

97
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:57,977
I'm not on fucking tilt.

98
00:07:57,978 --> 00:07:59,269
<i>Then he's testing you.</i>

99
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:00,604
<i>They're allowed to have tantrums.</i>

100
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:03,441
<i>We're not. So breathe in,
button down, and bottle up.</i>

101
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:06,276
<i>You need to be cool. Can you be cool, son?</i>

102
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:08,488
- Yes, sir. I can be cool.
<i>- Good.</i>

103
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:11,533
<i>- You want this, right?</i>
- Of course, I want this.

104
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:13,367
<i>Just stay the course</i>

105
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:14,703
<i>and this job is yours.</i>

106
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:17,914
Yeah, well...

107
00:08:28,091 --> 00:08:29,341
Shit.

108
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:30,552
Am I dead?

109
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:32,804
- What?
- You're wearing my ring.

110
00:08:33,471 --> 00:08:34,931
Is that supposed to be funny?

111
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:38,559
Hey, did I do something to piss you off?

112
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:40,019
'Cause if I did, I'm sorry.

113
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:42,396
You? Hal Jordan? Sorry?

114
00:08:42,397 --> 00:08:43,648
That's right.

115
00:08:44,149 --> 00:08:45,400
I must have a concussion.

116
00:08:46,151 --> 00:08:48,153
Wait a sec. Wait a sec.

117
00:08:48,695 --> 00:08:50,363
Let's start at the beginning.

118
00:08:51,406 --> 00:08:53,490
Who are you
and why are you wearing my ring?

119
00:08:53,491 --> 00:08:55,326
I'm John Stewart, your trainee.

120
00:08:56,411 --> 00:08:58,328
Lanterns don't have trainees
from their own sector.

121
00:08:58,329 --> 00:08:59,456
They do now.

122
00:09:00,832 --> 00:09:02,167
What year is it?

123
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:04,085
2016.

124
00:09:05,003 --> 00:09:06,004
Holy...

125
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,382
You want to tell me
what you think is going on?

126
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,051
I'm a backup
of Hal Jordan's consciousness,

127
00:09:12,052 --> 00:09:14,554
combined with the sentience of the ring,
I'm here to give myself a message.

128
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:18,016
- So you are Hal?
- No. Yes. Mostly. Ish.

129
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:21,101
Well, it's like when
you store yourself in the cloud,

130
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:22,352
only every once in a while,

131
00:09:22,353 --> 00:09:23,938
when you're needed
in the real world, you...

132
00:09:25,482 --> 00:09:27,649
Lanterns, they're required
to be uploaded weekly,

133
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:30,445
for posterity's sake, in case
something happens to us.

134
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:35,158
I should have taught you this.

135
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:38,410
I thought I was training you.

136
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:39,454
Yeah, I thought so, too.

137
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,414
When were you last backed up?

138
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:45,375
Evidently, ten years ago.
Listen, I need to find myself.

139
00:09:45,376 --> 00:09:47,169
- Where am I?
- Oh, you're three miles

140
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:49,129
up the street eating tacos.

141
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,673
Oh, good. You can fly us there, then.

142
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:54,135
I haven't...

143
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:56,930
taught you how to fly yet, have I?

144
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:02,810
I'll tell you what.

145
00:10:02,811 --> 00:10:05,939
You tell me what you want me to tell you.

146
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:08,817
Do I trust you?

147
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:13,696
I mean, you know, we...
You know, we get along?

148
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:15,907
We get along great.

149
00:10:20,578 --> 00:10:22,580
There's hail in Rushville, Nebraska.

150
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:27,669
- That's it?
- Well, I'll know what I mean.

151
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:41,850
Hey, it's Green Lantern!

152
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:45,394
- You're a legend, man.
- Thank you.

153
00:10:45,395 --> 00:10:47,020
- I want a selfie!
- Ask him!

154
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:48,523
Let the man breathe!

155
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:50,482
It's not a petting zoo.

156
00:10:50,483 --> 00:10:51,484
Come on.

157
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:54,027
I'll bring your food
to your table, Mr. Jordan.

158
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:55,988
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you.

159
00:10:55,989 --> 00:10:57,574
- All right, guys.
- Thanks very much. Thanks.

160
00:10:58,449 --> 00:10:59,534
Check it out!

161
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:02,995
I'm...

162
00:11:02,996 --> 00:11:04,664
Do you think that my daughter
could maybe...

163
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:07,625
Absolutely. Come here. Come on. Come here.

164
00:11:08,126 --> 00:11:09,293
There we go.

165
00:11:09,294 --> 00:11:10,795
All right.

166
00:11:11,379 --> 00:11:13,088
- Thank you.
- You're very welcome.

167
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:16,050
- She misses the suit.
- I didn't say that.

168
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:19,345
Tell your mom I still wear it
on special occasions.

169
00:11:19,846 --> 00:11:20,847
Yeah.

170
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:41,783
I could have fucking died.

171
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:43,953
You want me to train you,
I'm training you.

172
00:11:46,039 --> 00:11:47,498
How'd you save yourself?

173
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:49,667
What'd you make with the ring?

174
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:52,128
Bubble wrap.

175
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:56,298
- Oh, you're a genius.
- Yeah.

176
00:11:56,299 --> 00:11:57,675
Dessert's on the house.

177
00:11:58,218 --> 00:12:00,094
Well, thank you very much.

178
00:12:00,595 --> 00:12:03,473
Can I ask why only on special occasions?

179
00:12:06,517 --> 00:12:08,060
It's like when you're young and eager

180
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:10,145
and you like to prove yourself,
so you wear a tie

181
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:11,814
so people will take you seriously.

182
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,484
But when you get older and wiser...

183
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:19,405
you realize ties are a pain in the ass.

184
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:26,162
- Good one.
- Yeah. Good one.

185
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:29,332
Give me my ring.

186
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:37,131
You sent yourself a message, by the way.

187
00:12:38,216 --> 00:12:40,133
- What are you talking about?
- The ring.

188
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:41,594
Your backup consciousness.

189
00:12:42,095 --> 00:12:43,554
You were a lot nicer ten years ago.

190
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:44,764
What did I say?

191
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:47,892
"There's hail in Rushville, Nebraska."

192
00:12:48,685 --> 00:12:49,852
Pay the check.

193
00:12:59,529 --> 00:13:00,530
Motherfucker.

194
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:56,919
Sorry, no one's allowed in.

195
00:13:57,795 --> 00:13:59,963
Really? It seems like
the whole town's in there.

196
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:02,633
Oh, come on.
That's enough, don't you think?

197
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:05,844
John Stewart.

198
00:14:05,845 --> 00:14:07,764
I'm with Hal Jordan. We're partners.

199
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:10,682
I thought there was only
one Green Lantern.

200
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:14,062
- Well, technically, I'm in training.
- So like a sidekick?

201
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:20,610
Why don't you just make the call?

202
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,156
Hey, boss.

203
00:14:26,991 --> 00:14:28,201
There's another one.

204
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:31,496
<i>You fucking kidding me?</i>

205
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:34,706
<i>Tell him to stay on the fucking sidelines</i>

206
00:14:34,707 --> 00:14:36,334
<i>with that other fucking shithead.</i>

207
00:14:38,628 --> 00:14:39,629
Yes, ma'am.

208
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:45,635
What's the word?

209
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:50,014
Stay off the field.

210
00:15:09,826 --> 00:15:10,910
You ditched me.

211
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:14,329
I was testing you,
seeing if you had it in you

212
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:15,914
to get yourself here on your own.

213
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:17,999
You've been here six hours,

214
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,169
so why are they still processing
the scene?

215
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:23,588
Emergency services
from two different counties.

216
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:26,384
They're interviewing witnesses,
escorting them out ten at a time.

217
00:15:27,844 --> 00:15:29,846
It's a decidedly small-town pace.

218
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:33,014
I don't get it. You flew all the way here

219
00:15:33,015 --> 00:15:34,517
just to ride the bench.

220
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:39,772
The answer to that mystery
is heading right to you.

221
00:15:41,107 --> 00:15:42,358
Hey, Sheriff...

222
00:15:43,568 --> 00:15:45,653
Kane. John Stewart.

223
00:15:47,113 --> 00:15:48,281
Kerry.

224
00:15:48,823 --> 00:15:52,785
- John. Training under Hal.
- What an honor.

225
00:15:53,286 --> 00:15:55,162
'Cause it was certainly
an honor to meet him

226
00:15:55,163 --> 00:15:56,705
when he arrived.

227
00:15:56,706 --> 00:15:58,623
- You don't have jurisdiction.
- She's about to tell you

228
00:15:58,624 --> 00:15:59,791
we don't have jurisdiction.

229
00:15:59,792 --> 00:16:01,084
- You don't.
- I will.

230
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:02,753
I can't do this again.

231
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:07,382
Look, you're a big shot. Noted.
But your jurisdiction

232
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:10,051
only covers extraterrestrial events.

233
00:16:10,052 --> 00:16:13,221
This is pretty much
the definition of terrestrial.

234
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:14,973
These victims are going
to end up being aliens.

235
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:16,975
- Based on what?
- I have a feeling.

236
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:18,101
He has a feeling.

237
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:20,187
I have a very strong feeling.

238
00:16:20,188 --> 00:16:22,565
Well, then, by all means,
the scene is yours.

239
00:16:24,942 --> 00:16:29,530
Well, it seems kind of mellow
for a mass shooting, don't you think?

240
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,115
They're in shock.

241
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:34,035
Or nobody knows the victims.

242
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:37,538
Does anybody seem extra upset
to you down there?

243
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:42,710
You see anybody standing with the bodies?

244
00:16:43,878 --> 00:16:45,338
Say it with me now.

245
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,131
Aliens.

246
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:51,510
Look, I know you think you're helping,

247
00:16:51,511 --> 00:16:53,262
but you need to trust me.

248
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:56,598
These people are my friends.
They're my neighbors.

249
00:16:56,599 --> 00:16:59,477
They understand your job.
They know we're not alone.

250
00:16:59,977 --> 00:17:02,395
There's a difference
between hearing that on CNN

251
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:03,606
and seeing it up close.

252
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:06,149
If it ends up being the case,
we'll deal with it.

253
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:09,153
But until then, I'm trying
to keep the scene calm.

254
00:17:09,654 --> 00:17:14,242
So if you could do me a favor,
keep away from the news vans.

255
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:17,286
It was nice to meet you.

256
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:21,332
Now, if you'll both kindly stay
the fuck out of my way.

257
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:31,467
She's something incredible, isn't she?

258
00:17:31,968 --> 00:17:33,427
I think she hates your guts.

259
00:17:34,804 --> 00:17:36,806
Yeah, but it's the way she hates them.

260
00:17:42,562 --> 00:17:43,937
So, what's going on here?

261
00:17:43,938 --> 00:17:46,357
Well, if I'm not mistaken--

262
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:49,569
Why don't you tell me?

263
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:57,493
Looks to me like Rushville scored
a game-winning field goal.

264
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:02,164
<i>Kicking block is still out there.</i>

265
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:04,166
<i>Fence is broken.</i>

266
00:18:04,709 --> 00:18:07,336
<i>My guess is home fans rushed the field.</i>

267
00:18:07,837 --> 00:18:09,087
<i>This being a rivalry,</i>

268
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:11,756
<i>a few visitor fans wander onto the field.</i>

269
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:14,468
<i>This being Nebraska,
more than a few are carrying.</i>

270
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:18,388
<i>You got four dead,
all in visitor sweatshirts.</i>

271
00:18:18,389 --> 00:18:23,477
And still none of this explains why you
think it has anything to do with aliens.

272
00:18:27,607 --> 00:18:30,025
You know, I've been doing this job
since you were a baby.

273
00:18:30,026 --> 00:18:32,193
I'm the only person
on this whole goddamn planet

274
00:18:32,194 --> 00:18:33,695
that's ever done this job.

275
00:18:33,696 --> 00:18:36,406
I say I got a fucking feeling,
I got a fucking feeling, Junior.

276
00:18:36,407 --> 00:18:38,451
"There's hail in Rushville, Nebraska."

277
00:18:39,076 --> 00:18:41,244
You've been monitoring this exact spot.

278
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:42,871
"Hail" obviously means aliens.

279
00:18:42,872 --> 00:18:44,874
Christ, they even sound the fucking same.

280
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:47,959
So we both know this is more
than just a feeling.

281
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,295
- Do we?
- Yeah, we do.

282
00:18:50,588 --> 00:18:52,131
Here's all you need to know.

283
00:18:52,715 --> 00:18:54,050
This is my job.

284
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:56,927
As long as I'm alive,
that ain't changing.

285
00:18:57,428 --> 00:18:59,679
And I don't plan on dying anytime soon,

286
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:02,098
so why don't you do yourself a big favor

287
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:04,435
and take a nice long, deep breath, Junior?

288
00:19:14,904 --> 00:19:15,905
Fuck.

289
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:18,616
I think one of them is still here.

290
00:19:19,492 --> 00:19:21,159
Yeah, the one in the short-sleeved shirt.

291
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,577
Been clocking him since I got here,

292
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:25,414
trying to figure out why he didn't bolt,
and what he still wants here.

293
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:27,166
You told the sheriff?

294
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:29,251
Of course not.

295
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,087
But it's her crime scene.

296
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,756
That's how you'd play this
if you had the ring?

297
00:19:34,757 --> 00:19:35,840
Yeah.

298
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:37,385
I respect the chain of command.

299
00:19:40,304 --> 00:19:42,264
Well, by all means, go respect it.

300
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:51,816
Would you excuse me?

301
00:19:54,110 --> 00:19:56,028
Hey, shithead.

302
00:19:56,529 --> 00:19:59,656
What part of stay the fuck away,
was confusing?

303
00:19:59,657 --> 00:20:01,032
There's something you need to see.

304
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:02,283
If you're about to tell me

305
00:20:02,284 --> 00:20:03,993
about the redneck in the short sleeves

306
00:20:03,994 --> 00:20:05,453
who ditched his only warm clothes

307
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:07,539
so we wouldn't put him
with the other victims,

308
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:09,666
I'm trying to make sure
he doesn't get spooked

309
00:20:09,667 --> 00:20:12,253
and start shooting the place up
like his dead friends.

310
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:17,132
I just fucked up, didn't I?

311
00:20:17,133 --> 00:20:18,801
I suspect you did.

312
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:28,978
Fuck.

313
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,063
- You got him?
- Sure.

314
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:04,406
- I need to interrogate him.
- Like fucking hell you do.

315
00:22:08,244 --> 00:22:09,245
Hi.

316
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:11,705
- Yeah.
- You thirsty?

317
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:44,655
Howdy, fellas.

318
00:22:50,619 --> 00:22:53,288
Hey, can I have another,
another, and another?

319
00:22:53,289 --> 00:22:54,373
Sure thing.

320
00:22:55,833 --> 00:22:58,209
Did you just use that ring
to counterfeit money?

321
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:01,379
No. I manifested money
with the power of my will.

322
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,131
Oh, wow. But you couldn't manifest

323
00:23:03,132 --> 00:23:05,467
something for the guy I was chasing.
Got it.

324
00:23:06,260 --> 00:23:08,012
This ring is a dangerous weapon.

325
00:23:08,971 --> 00:23:12,099
When and if to use it,
that's the whole ball game, Junior.

326
00:23:14,268 --> 00:23:16,728
Tell me how you got it, the ring.

327
00:23:16,729 --> 00:23:17,937
You know how I got it.

328
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:20,149
Yeah, but I mean,
what I know can't be true, right?

329
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,358
Well, I got it the old-fashioned way.

330
00:23:22,359 --> 00:23:25,613
- I sure as hell didn't interview for it.
- Oh, well, shit, maybe you should have.

331
00:23:26,989 --> 00:23:29,574
I mean, power like that,
shouldn't you have to work for it,

332
00:23:29,575 --> 00:23:30,950
excel, prove yourself,

333
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:33,620
instead of just
getting randomly selected?

334
00:23:33,621 --> 00:23:35,663
Why do you give a shit how I got my ring?

335
00:23:35,664 --> 00:23:38,500
Because I think that's why
we're in goddamn Nebraska.

336
00:23:41,503 --> 00:23:44,047
I was a couple years
into being a test pilot.

337
00:23:44,048 --> 00:23:45,340
You know, middle of the night,

338
00:23:45,341 --> 00:23:46,925
I'm sleeping off about nine too many,

339
00:23:46,926 --> 00:23:48,636
still had my boots and jeans on.

340
00:23:50,554 --> 00:23:52,765
All of a sudden,
my room starts to vibrate.

341
00:23:54,308 --> 00:23:55,559
I open my eyes,

342
00:23:56,060 --> 00:23:57,894
and I'm in a big fucking bubble.

343
00:23:57,895 --> 00:23:59,813
A big fucking green bubble.

344
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:02,815
This green bubble floats me up out of bed.

345
00:24:02,816 --> 00:24:04,275
Next thing I know, there's a voice

346
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:05,777
running through my entire body,

347
00:24:05,778 --> 00:24:07,613
bones, teeth, heart, the whole deal.

348
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:09,323
And it says to me...

349
00:24:11,325 --> 00:24:12,660
"Are you afraid?"

350
00:24:13,911 --> 00:24:17,872
I say, "No. I'm not afraid."

351
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:19,041
Wham!

352
00:24:19,917 --> 00:24:22,710
Yanks me out the window across the sky
like a fish getting reeled in.

353
00:24:22,711 --> 00:24:24,713
Couple hundred miles in about ten seconds.

354
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:27,006
I fly fighter jets.

355
00:24:27,007 --> 00:24:29,092
I have an excellent sense
of airspeed and bearing.

356
00:24:29,093 --> 00:24:32,054
That's how I know exactly
where that green bubble set me down.

357
00:24:32,638 --> 00:24:33,721
Nebraska.

358
00:24:33,722 --> 00:24:36,432
Not more than 20 miles
from where we sit right now.

359
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:38,811
Which is middle of fucking nowhere.

360
00:24:39,353 --> 00:24:41,730
Thus, an excellent place
to crash a spaceship.

361
00:24:44,566 --> 00:24:45,609
There he was.

362
00:24:46,318 --> 00:24:47,860
Right in front of me.

363
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:48,862
The pilot.

364
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:51,406
Bonafide fucking alien.

365
00:24:51,407 --> 00:24:54,450
Pink and bald, coughing up
glow-in-the-dark blood.

366
00:24:54,451 --> 00:24:56,078
It was pretty fucking intense.

367
00:25:03,919 --> 00:25:06,296
Hey, you think you're funny?

368
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:09,173
So Pinko starts talking.

369
00:25:09,174 --> 00:25:12,219
And it comes out all clicks and gurgles.
He's dying.

370
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:15,973
And he gives me his ring. This ring.

371
00:25:16,849 --> 00:25:18,558
And when I put it on,

372
00:25:18,559 --> 00:25:20,894
I can understand
every fucking word he says.

373
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:24,314
"My name is Abin Sur,

374
00:25:25,274 --> 00:25:28,402
responsible for maintaining
the peace and sovereignty

375
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:30,863
of Sector 2814.

376
00:25:32,948 --> 00:25:35,034
And this responsibility is now yours,

377
00:25:35,868 --> 00:25:38,495
as the ring has chosen you
to be my successor."

378
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:42,373
Now, fuck, did I know
what sovereignty meant?

379
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:45,335
Hell no, I didn't.
And then he said two more words,

380
00:25:46,045 --> 00:25:47,254
his last words.

381
00:25:47,838 --> 00:25:49,297
And he kind of whispered 'em,

382
00:25:49,298 --> 00:25:51,507
so I'm never really sure
whether he said "Good luck"

383
00:25:51,508 --> 00:25:52,593
or "Ah, fuck."

384
00:25:53,135 --> 00:25:55,762
Anyway, it turns out Earth's way off grid,

385
00:25:55,763 --> 00:25:58,432
out of their jurisdiction.
Galactic fucking backwater.

386
00:25:59,016 --> 00:26:01,518
A human getting a ring,
isn't it a fucking fluke?

387
00:26:03,604 --> 00:26:05,730
The big, blue bosses,
they'd never wanted any Lantern

388
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:07,649
coming near our little shithole planet.

389
00:26:08,692 --> 00:26:12,654
And that's why my gut always told me
that crash was no accident.

390
00:26:13,197 --> 00:26:15,324
When it says there's a shitstorm en route,

391
00:26:15,866 --> 00:26:19,077
I make sure there's a lookout
to tell me when it's fucking coming.

392
00:26:19,078 --> 00:26:20,537
The Halogram.

393
00:26:22,372 --> 00:26:24,124
Halogram. That's clever.

394
00:26:24,625 --> 00:26:26,460
- Thank you.
- It's not that clever.

395
00:26:29,505 --> 00:26:32,216
Hey, Jordan! Ass-face!

396
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,175
You ignoring me?

397
00:26:34,176 --> 00:26:36,803
So help me God, if that song
plays one more time,

398
00:26:36,804 --> 00:26:39,098
I'm gonna put you
inside that fucking jukebox!

399
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:43,476
Hal, I think he's talking to you.

400
00:26:43,477 --> 00:26:44,645
Yeah, I hear him.

401
00:26:45,187 --> 00:26:46,355
You want to fight?

402
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:49,608
You want to go to jail.

403
00:26:51,193 --> 00:26:54,070
You want to go to jail
so you can talk to that guy

404
00:26:54,071 --> 00:26:55,822
that Mrs. Sheriff
doesn't want you to talk to.

405
00:26:55,823 --> 00:26:56,907
Not guy.

406
00:26:57,741 --> 00:27:00,076
- Alien.
- This is a stupid plan.

407
00:27:00,077 --> 00:27:02,246
- I've had stupider.
- That I do not doubt.

408
00:27:05,999 --> 00:27:07,835
All right. Here we go.

409
00:27:14,007 --> 00:27:17,677
Look, it's gonna look like they're really
kicking the shit out of me,

410
00:27:17,678 --> 00:27:20,513
so you're gonna be tempted to jump in,
but I need you to stay right here.

411
00:27:20,514 --> 00:27:21,765
Will do. You got it.

412
00:27:25,060 --> 00:27:26,228
Thanks.

413
00:27:32,651 --> 00:27:34,153
Hey, fellas.

414
00:27:35,154 --> 00:27:36,613
Tell me something, would you?

415
00:27:37,322 --> 00:27:40,074
What the fuck is your problem
with roller skates?

416
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:42,410
Look, pretty boy. Show me what you got.

417
00:27:42,411 --> 00:27:44,370
Oh, my. You look like my sister.

418
00:27:44,371 --> 00:27:45,538
God bless ya. Now what?

419
00:27:45,539 --> 00:27:46,998
What the fuck are you talking about?

420
00:27:46,999 --> 00:27:48,292
You gonna say yes?

421
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:52,629
He didn't get down on one knee,
but a ring's a ring.

422
00:27:53,714 --> 00:27:56,174
No, I don't think he wants me
to have this ring.

423
00:27:56,175 --> 00:27:57,301
Ever.

424
00:27:58,051 --> 00:28:00,761
- But he gave it to you.
- I reckon he's testing me.

425
00:28:00,762 --> 00:28:01,972
Testing you how?

426
00:28:07,686 --> 00:28:10,063
- Who gives a shit?
- Come on, bring it on.

427
00:28:10,564 --> 00:28:12,274
- What are you drinking, stranger?
- Coke.

428
00:28:12,858 --> 00:28:14,525
- Coke and what?
- Coke and Coke.

429
00:28:14,526 --> 00:28:16,194
Don't tell me you're a teetotaler.

430
00:28:16,195 --> 00:28:17,278
No, I'm just...

431
00:28:17,279 --> 00:28:18,905
I'm just on the job.

432
00:28:18,906 --> 00:28:20,490
Being a space cop.

433
00:28:22,576 --> 00:28:24,536
Who told you I was a space cop?

434
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,580
I mean, your partner is one.

435
00:28:27,247 --> 00:28:28,707
Figured you are too.

436
00:28:29,333 --> 00:28:31,501
He's not my partner. I'm his trainee.

437
00:28:33,462 --> 00:28:35,129
How many trainees does he have?

438
00:28:35,130 --> 00:28:37,381
- Just me.
- Why'd he pick you?

439
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:39,092
He didn't. Our bosses did.

440
00:28:40,052 --> 00:28:43,222
Space cops have bosses?

441
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:48,477
Come on, everybody's got bosses, you know?

442
00:28:51,772 --> 00:28:56,651
So, once you're trained,
then you're an official space cop too?

443
00:28:56,652 --> 00:29:00,071
Well, the way it works
is Earth has one Lantern.

444
00:29:00,072 --> 00:29:04,743
So I'm just being trained
in case anything happens to Jordan.

445
00:29:05,369 --> 00:29:07,203
So you're the backup quarterback.

446
00:29:07,204 --> 00:29:08,247
I'm patient.

447
00:29:09,081 --> 00:29:10,123
No, you're not.

448
00:29:11,541 --> 00:29:14,211
All right, idiots. Break it up!

449
00:29:16,088 --> 00:29:17,922
- Get out!
- Do I gotta call your mom again?

450
00:29:17,923 --> 00:29:19,508
Get out of here. Now!

451
00:29:32,271 --> 00:29:34,021
Let's go.
Let's go, sweetness.

452
00:29:34,022 --> 00:29:35,274
Get him out of here!

453
00:29:35,941 --> 00:29:37,316
Yeah, yeah.

454
00:29:37,317 --> 00:29:38,902
Nice talking to you, stranger.

455
00:29:41,363 --> 00:29:42,655
I'm John.

456
00:29:42,656 --> 00:29:44,241
Walk me to my truck, John?

457
00:30:12,519 --> 00:30:14,062
You gonna give me a lecture?

458
00:30:14,771 --> 00:30:15,772
No.

459
00:30:17,190 --> 00:30:18,817
I'm gonna give you a light.

460
00:30:32,247 --> 00:30:34,499
Because no comment means no comment.

461
00:30:35,667 --> 00:30:39,129
I'm not gonna talk about
an active investigation, you know that.

462
00:30:40,589 --> 00:30:41,757
Okay.

463
00:30:42,257 --> 00:30:43,258
Good.

464
00:30:44,217 --> 00:30:45,719
Tell Barb I said hey.

465
00:30:48,847 --> 00:30:51,724
I take it you're here
to bail out your buddy?

466
00:30:51,725 --> 00:30:52,975
Want some coffee?

467
00:30:52,976 --> 00:30:55,645
I am, and no thank you.

468
00:30:56,188 --> 00:30:57,438
He's in a bit of a mood

469
00:30:57,439 --> 00:30:59,900
because I locked him in our broom closet.

470
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:03,652
It's almost as if he wanted
to get arrested

471
00:31:03,653 --> 00:31:06,155
so I'd throw him in jail
next to the suspect

472
00:31:06,156 --> 00:31:07,908
I told him he couldn't talk to.

473
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:10,744
I did tell him it was a stupid plan.

474
00:31:11,244 --> 00:31:13,496
You should have told him louder.

475
00:31:13,497 --> 00:31:16,666
Well, listen, may I take
my stupid friend home?

476
00:31:17,793 --> 00:31:19,753
Not until he's arraigned.

477
00:31:23,423 --> 00:31:24,757
Really?

478
00:31:24,758 --> 00:31:27,093
...and eight counts of aggravated assault

479
00:31:27,094 --> 00:31:28,427
and resisting arrest.

480
00:31:28,428 --> 00:31:29,804
How does the defendant plead?

481
00:31:29,805 --> 00:31:32,432
With all due respect, Your Honor, come on.

482
00:31:33,350 --> 00:31:34,433
"Come on"?

483
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:36,394
Look, I'm just trying
to question a suspect

484
00:31:36,395 --> 00:31:38,270
in the course
of a very serious investigation,

485
00:31:38,271 --> 00:31:40,065
- which I--
- Ah, an investigation.

486
00:31:40,690 --> 00:31:42,149
Am I to understand, sir,

487
00:31:42,150 --> 00:31:44,485
that you are a law enforcement official?

488
00:31:44,486 --> 00:31:46,529
And if so, could you kindly
state for the record

489
00:31:46,530 --> 00:31:48,281
which agency you represent?

490
00:31:49,533 --> 00:31:50,908
I'm Green Lantern.

491
00:31:50,909 --> 00:31:52,618
I didn't ask who you were.

492
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:55,746
I asked which bureau you are an agent of.

493
00:31:55,747 --> 00:31:56,997
I'm Green Lantern,

494
00:31:56,998 --> 00:31:58,834
and I'm an agent of...

495
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:01,293
the Green Lantern, so.

496
00:32:01,294 --> 00:32:04,296
Look, I introduced myself
to Lady Justice back here

497
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:07,842
when I got to the crime scene,
and I deferred to her jurisdiction.

498
00:32:07,843 --> 00:32:09,386
Is that accurate, Sheriff?

499
00:32:09,886 --> 00:32:12,889
Yeah, but the deference
was pretty cheeky, Your Honor.

500
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:15,141
You cheeky, Mr. Jordan?

501
00:32:15,142 --> 00:32:16,893
Yeah, don't answer that.

502
00:32:18,061 --> 00:32:20,646
William Macon for the defense, Your Honor.

503
00:32:20,647 --> 00:32:22,565
- Sorry I'm late.
- Mr. Macon.

504
00:32:22,566 --> 00:32:25,526
The defendant has chosen
to represent himself.

505
00:32:25,527 --> 00:32:27,027
That's only because he doesn't understand

506
00:32:27,028 --> 00:32:30,156
he's being made an example of,
which, Your Honor,

507
00:32:30,157 --> 00:32:32,409
is absurd given Mr. Jordan is a hero.

508
00:32:33,326 --> 00:32:36,370
Granted, he hasn't formally retained my--

509
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:38,914
- You're hired. He's hired.
- Fantastic.

510
00:32:38,915 --> 00:32:41,333
The defense enters a plea of not guilty

511
00:32:41,334 --> 00:32:44,003
and asks Your Honor
to set reasonable bail,

512
00:32:44,004 --> 00:32:47,757
even understanding Mr. Jordan
is... technically a flight risk.

513
00:32:48,258 --> 00:32:49,259
Because...

514
00:32:50,051 --> 00:32:51,094
he can fly.

515
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:53,513
Who is this guy?

516
00:32:54,014 --> 00:32:55,222
My husband.

517
00:32:55,223 --> 00:32:57,600
I'm setting bail at 100,000 dollars.

518
00:32:57,601 --> 00:32:59,728
- Oh, come on.
- Two hundred thousand.

519
00:33:00,395 --> 00:33:03,231
Now you know the price
of each "come on," Mr. Jordan.

520
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:06,609
- Shall we try another?
- No, that's understood.

521
00:33:06,610 --> 00:33:08,152
And thank you, Your Honor.

522
00:33:08,153 --> 00:33:11,031
My father will have the check
to your clerk by lunch.

523
00:33:11,531 --> 00:33:14,326
All right, then.
Mr. Jordan, don't leave town.

524
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:15,994
We're adjourned.

525
00:33:19,122 --> 00:33:21,290
- Thanks for the save.
- Oh, truly an honor.

526
00:33:21,291 --> 00:33:23,667
But I tend to find
that strangers who give me

527
00:33:23,668 --> 00:33:25,044
a couple hundred thousand dollars,

528
00:33:25,045 --> 00:33:27,797
no strings attached,
usually turn out to be bad guys.

529
00:33:28,632 --> 00:33:31,133
But there are
strings attached, Mr. Jordan.

530
00:33:31,134 --> 00:33:35,054
My father would love to have supper
with you this evening. He's a huge fan,

531
00:33:35,055 --> 00:33:37,890
and someone I think
you'll find like-minded.

532
00:33:37,891 --> 00:33:39,141
What are you doing, Billy?

533
00:33:39,142 --> 00:33:43,063
I was just inviting Mr. Jordan
up to the ranch tonight, honey.

534
00:33:44,898 --> 00:33:46,357
They're married.

535
00:33:46,358 --> 00:33:49,443
Course, they are.
Small town, everyone's related.

536
00:33:49,444 --> 00:33:50,528
Oh.

537
00:33:50,529 --> 00:33:53,280
I'd be offended if that wasn't
absolutely true.

538
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:54,823
Billy Macon, you must be John.

539
00:33:54,824 --> 00:33:56,159
- Yes, sir.
- You like barbecue?

540
00:33:56,743 --> 00:33:57,910
Junior here's a vegan.

541
00:33:57,911 --> 00:33:59,995
He doesn't believe in anything
that causes enjoyment.

542
00:33:59,996 --> 00:34:01,705
But we'd love to come to supper.

543
00:34:01,706 --> 00:34:04,501
Yeah, well, only if it's okay
with the sheriff.

544
00:34:05,585 --> 00:34:07,003
The more the merrier.

545
00:34:56,261 --> 00:34:57,262
Militia?

546
00:34:59,347 --> 00:35:03,268
Walks like a duck, shoots an AR-15
like a duck, blah, blah, blah, duck.

547
00:35:23,413 --> 00:35:24,623
Evening.

548
00:35:25,415 --> 00:35:27,292
- So glad you could make it.
- How you doing?

549
00:35:27,417 --> 00:35:29,877
- This is our boy, Noah.
- All right. How you doing, Noah?

550
00:35:29,878 --> 00:35:31,462
Noah, this is Mr. Stewart and Mr. Jordan.

551
00:35:31,463 --> 00:35:32,505
Noah.

552
00:35:33,298 --> 00:35:34,632
Offense or defense?

553
00:35:34,633 --> 00:35:36,051
Wherever they need me, sir.

554
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:38,637
Team player. Good man.

555
00:35:40,764 --> 00:35:43,557
Oh, sorry. I got to take this.

556
00:35:43,558 --> 00:35:45,809
Dad's waiting in the kitchen
for you gentlemen.

557
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:48,062
Noah, come with me
and help Grandma set up.

558
00:35:48,063 --> 00:35:49,064
Hey.

559
00:35:50,649 --> 00:35:51,650
Yeah.

560
00:35:56,279 --> 00:35:57,364
How about a beer?

561
00:35:59,699 --> 00:36:00,867
God, yes.

562
00:36:02,077 --> 00:36:03,078
Oh, here.

563
00:36:19,719 --> 00:36:22,847
My father-in-law's got paper on you
and you haven't even met him yet.

564
00:36:23,765 --> 00:36:25,642
He's not a man you want to owe.

565
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:27,727
Sounds like a woman in debt.

566
00:36:31,606 --> 00:36:32,691
It's not too late.

567
00:36:33,191 --> 00:36:34,775
You can just fly on home,

568
00:36:34,776 --> 00:36:36,985
spare yourself the moment
not too long from now

569
00:36:36,986 --> 00:36:39,572
when you wish
you'd never come to this place.

570
00:36:41,074 --> 00:36:42,075
No.

571
00:36:49,374 --> 00:36:50,834
Well...

572
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:54,294
Exciting enough Hal Jordan just
walked into my kitchen,

573
00:36:54,295 --> 00:36:55,713
but with a bag of beer?

574
00:36:55,714 --> 00:36:56,964
I'm truly blessed.

575
00:36:56,965 --> 00:36:59,466
Least I can do. This is John.

576
00:36:59,467 --> 00:37:01,051
John, Will Macon.

577
00:37:01,052 --> 00:37:03,679
I'd shake, but my hands
are all gunky with meat.

578
00:37:03,680 --> 00:37:05,640
Word on the street is you don't partake.

579
00:37:06,182 --> 00:37:07,975
Ordered you up some tofu steaks.

580
00:37:07,976 --> 00:37:11,312
- Hope that'll do you.
- Oh, that's very kind. I appreciate it.

581
00:37:12,647 --> 00:37:16,984
And I appreciate your service, sir.
Marine sniper. Color me impressed.

582
00:37:16,985 --> 00:37:18,820
Oh, looked me up.

583
00:37:19,446 --> 00:37:20,822
You didn't look me up?

584
00:37:22,365 --> 00:37:23,616
Jesus.

585
00:37:24,117 --> 00:37:26,243
Walking into unknown territory,
even with a weapon

586
00:37:26,244 --> 00:37:29,455
of mass destruction on your finger,
that's either trust or arrogance.

587
00:37:29,456 --> 00:37:31,081
Well, he's trust. I'm arrogance.

588
00:37:31,082 --> 00:37:32,541
I don't trust anybody.

589
00:37:32,542 --> 00:37:33,877
Man after my own heart.

590
00:37:35,712 --> 00:37:37,504
You got a nice place here, Will.

591
00:37:37,505 --> 00:37:38,840
Yeah, it is, isn't it?

592
00:37:39,674 --> 00:37:43,135
Alas, not mine. I'm just a caretaker.

593
00:37:43,136 --> 00:37:45,180
Mind me asking who you caretake it for?

594
00:37:45,722 --> 00:37:47,097
I don't mind at all.

595
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:50,559
Regrettably, my NDA
restricts me from discussing

596
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:52,520
or IDing my employer.

597
00:37:53,605 --> 00:37:54,939
Because of the government.

598
00:37:55,857 --> 00:37:56,940
I'm sorry?

599
00:37:56,941 --> 00:37:58,650
The government.
I'm guessing the government,

600
00:37:58,651 --> 00:38:00,194
they're probably watching your boss,

601
00:38:00,195 --> 00:38:02,988
biding their time
before they raid this compound,

602
00:38:02,989 --> 00:38:04,531
take his guns and rights away.

603
00:38:04,532 --> 00:38:07,284
You think we bailed you out
so we could enlist you

604
00:38:07,285 --> 00:38:08,912
in some whackadoo war with the feds?

605
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:12,998
Well, why else would you bail me out?

606
00:38:12,999 --> 00:38:15,210
Because of the goddamn aliens, son.

607
00:38:16,002 --> 00:38:17,128
Why the fuck else?

608
00:38:21,007 --> 00:38:24,719
Man, the whole world flipped out
when you first came on the scene.

609
00:38:25,553 --> 00:38:27,430
Makes sense, seeing what you can do.

610
00:38:28,097 --> 00:38:29,808
But it kind of buried the lede.

611
00:38:31,226 --> 00:38:33,812
There are thousands of planets out there
with intelligent life.

612
00:38:34,687 --> 00:38:37,940
And here we sit,
low-hanging fruit of the galaxy,

613
00:38:37,941 --> 00:38:39,858
just waiting to get gobbled up.

614
00:38:39,859 --> 00:38:43,238
This land we're on right now,
it was Kiowa, then Sioux,

615
00:38:43,863 --> 00:38:46,282
but across the ocean boats were coming.

616
00:38:48,034 --> 00:38:50,995
Anyways, as someone
who's spent time in the galaxy,

617
00:38:51,663 --> 00:38:53,455
it's a pretty peaceful place out there.

618
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:55,959
Well, what do they need space cops for?

619
00:38:59,754 --> 00:39:04,050
Look, I'm not some isolationist crackpot
with his head in the sand,

620
00:39:04,759 --> 00:39:06,510
but I am a student of history.

621
00:39:06,511 --> 00:39:08,637
Colonization is ugly from any angle,

622
00:39:08,638 --> 00:39:13,893
but I tell you, it is particularly bleak
if you're the one getting colonized.

623
00:39:14,811 --> 00:39:17,604
This all, call it an ounce of prevention.

624
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:19,273
Seems like a bit more than an ounce.

625
00:39:19,274 --> 00:39:20,316
My point is,

626
00:39:20,942 --> 00:39:22,568
I believe the gentleman cooling his heels

627
00:39:22,569 --> 00:39:25,363
in the sheriff's pokey,
he's part of an advanced team.

628
00:39:26,531 --> 00:39:28,490
And I'd ask you
what your reason to believe is,

629
00:39:28,491 --> 00:39:30,702
but I'm guessing it's covered by your NDA.

630
00:39:31,703 --> 00:39:33,954
My daughter-in-law says
you're not that bright.

631
00:39:33,955 --> 00:39:36,332
Your daughter-in-law's what's
holding me up from talking to that fella.

632
00:39:38,209 --> 00:39:40,420
All right. I can clear that brush.

633
00:39:41,588 --> 00:39:42,714
In exchange for?

634
00:39:44,132 --> 00:39:45,133
Let's eat.

635
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:09,324
You're aiming.

636
00:40:09,866 --> 00:40:10,867
Sorry, sir?

637
00:40:12,243 --> 00:40:13,244
Don't aim.

638
00:40:13,745 --> 00:40:16,706
Just imagine it going through.

639
00:40:20,251 --> 00:40:21,294
Try again.

640
00:40:23,463 --> 00:40:24,964
Hey, don't force it.

641
00:40:25,465 --> 00:40:26,549
Just imagine.

642
00:40:37,727 --> 00:40:38,770
Hey!

643
00:40:39,270 --> 00:40:40,313
What'd I say?

644
00:40:40,939 --> 00:40:41,981
What'd I just say?

645
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:44,275
That was great.

646
00:40:44,901 --> 00:40:46,234
How'd you know that?

647
00:40:46,235 --> 00:40:49,697
So, my dad used to shoot apples
off my head.

648
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:51,490
Grandma!

649
00:40:51,491 --> 00:40:53,033
Grandma, I got one through!

650
00:40:53,034 --> 00:40:54,202
Show me, sweetheart.

651
00:40:59,749 --> 00:41:00,792
You live here?

652
00:41:03,419 --> 00:41:04,420
Zoe Macon.

653
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,009
Now you have my name.

654
00:41:11,594 --> 00:41:13,261
Come on, sweetheart.
Let's go find everyone.

655
00:41:13,262 --> 00:41:14,514
- All right.
- Come on.

656
00:41:20,019 --> 00:41:23,481
Well, we drank all your beer,
but put together some leftovers for you.

657
00:41:24,273 --> 00:41:26,484
- Much obliged.
- And I talked to Kerry.

658
00:41:26,985 --> 00:41:28,568
Since you and I have common interests,

659
00:41:28,569 --> 00:41:31,030
she's willing to let you chat with
the suspect first thing in the morning.

660
00:41:31,990 --> 00:41:33,074
Well...

661
00:41:36,703 --> 00:41:38,413
You know, that's the thing, Will.

662
00:41:38,913 --> 00:41:40,665
I don't know what your interests are.

663
00:41:41,541 --> 00:41:43,626
Two of my boys
almost got killed last night

664
00:41:44,168 --> 00:41:46,838
in a shootout with men
no one's ever seen before.

665
00:41:47,839 --> 00:41:51,134
How about we both want to protect
the planet from anybody not born on it?

666
00:41:54,470 --> 00:41:56,514
Hope I didn't mess up your tofu, soldier.

667
00:41:57,640 --> 00:41:58,641
No, sir.

668
00:41:59,475 --> 00:42:00,560
It was delicious.

669
00:42:01,060 --> 00:42:02,227
Good.

670
00:42:02,228 --> 00:42:04,272
Nothing better than eating off
another man's grill.

671
00:42:07,275 --> 00:42:08,526
Good night, gentlemen.

672
00:42:16,034 --> 00:42:17,035
Hey.

673
00:42:17,660 --> 00:42:18,953
What was that all about?

674
00:42:22,206 --> 00:42:23,750
I might have slept with his wife.

675
00:42:24,625 --> 00:42:25,668
Might have?

676
00:42:28,463 --> 00:42:30,465
I definitely slept with his wife.

677
00:42:32,925 --> 00:42:34,302
And he knows?

678
00:42:35,636 --> 00:42:36,637
Apparently.

679
00:42:37,597 --> 00:42:40,433
Jesus Christ,
we've only been here 24 hours.

680
00:42:41,976 --> 00:42:43,144
I'm impressed.

681
00:43:00,328 --> 00:43:01,454
We said 9:00.

682
00:43:02,246 --> 00:43:03,455
What time is it?

683
00:43:03,456 --> 00:43:04,749
Not 9:00.

684
00:43:11,839 --> 00:43:13,965
His name's Waylon Sanders.

685
00:43:13,966 --> 00:43:16,968
Commercial-licensed
truck driver. Called his boss,

686
00:43:16,969 --> 00:43:19,514
says he's worked for him
almost five years now.

687
00:43:20,348 --> 00:43:23,642
Aliens are good at getting IDs
and paying people to lie for them.

688
00:43:23,643 --> 00:43:25,603
He's just a dipshit from Kimball.

689
00:43:26,229 --> 00:43:29,107
They took X-rays at the hospital
for his busted nose.

690
00:43:29,607 --> 00:43:33,528
All organs accounted for.
No hidden antennas.

691
00:43:34,195 --> 00:43:35,987
The plural for antenna is antennae.

692
00:43:35,988 --> 00:43:37,865
What's the plural for eat shit?

693
00:43:40,868 --> 00:43:43,078
Junior, tell the sheriff here
how many species currently

694
00:43:43,079 --> 00:43:45,038
have the technology to pass as human.

695
00:43:45,039 --> 00:43:49,627
Fourteen. MRIs, X-rays, blood work.
Nothing down here can tell the difference.

696
00:43:50,461 --> 00:43:52,672
- So you can't prove it.
- I can make him confess.

697
00:43:53,339 --> 00:43:56,008
If you lay a finger on him,
you're back in front of the judge.

698
00:43:56,634 --> 00:43:59,052
That includes whacking him
with giant green phone books

699
00:43:59,053 --> 00:44:01,596
or whatever you magic up
from your conjuring ring.

700
00:44:01,597 --> 00:44:02,889
I wouldn't dare.

701
00:44:02,890 --> 00:44:05,350
- Ten minutes.
- I only need five.

702
00:44:05,351 --> 00:44:07,061
- Am I'm coming in with you?
- You are not.

703
00:44:15,611 --> 00:44:16,946
Alien my ass.

704
00:44:19,115 --> 00:44:20,658
You know, we're all aliens.

705
00:44:21,367 --> 00:44:23,578
Just depends which planet
you're standing on.

706
00:44:24,954 --> 00:44:26,581
<i>Would you like a cup of coffee?</i>

707
00:44:27,081 --> 00:44:28,541
<i>- No, thank you.
- All right.</i>

708
00:44:30,543 --> 00:44:33,254
Yeah, I imagine you just
want to phone home, or...

709
00:44:33,921 --> 00:44:35,756
- get home, I bet.
- Yes, sir.

710
00:44:37,008 --> 00:44:38,384
And home is Kimball?

711
00:44:38,926 --> 00:44:40,969
Well, I mean, I'm on the road
most of the year,

712
00:44:40,970 --> 00:44:43,263
but Kimball's where
I hang my hat. Yes, sir.

713
00:44:43,264 --> 00:44:46,349
"Hang your hat."
What a delightful human expression.

714
00:44:46,350 --> 00:44:49,811
And well, if you're in town for
the big game, it must be a big rivalry.

715
00:44:49,812 --> 00:44:53,941
I mean, Kimball's, what, that's a two,
two-and-a-half-hour drive?

716
00:44:54,734 --> 00:44:56,067
Yeah, sorry about that.

717
00:44:56,068 --> 00:44:58,153
I just, you know, I--
I love football, though,

718
00:44:58,154 --> 00:44:59,905
and it's the home team.

719
00:44:59,906 --> 00:45:02,033
Yeah. I love football, too.

720
00:45:03,618 --> 00:45:06,287
When did Nebraska win
its first national championship?

721
00:45:07,038 --> 00:45:08,247
<i>Sorry?</i>

722
00:45:09,040 --> 00:45:11,333
<i>You love football. You're from Nebraska.</i>

723
00:45:11,334 --> 00:45:13,836
Huskers' first championship,
when was that?

724
00:45:15,755 --> 00:45:20,885
- Yeah, it was 1970, Bob Devaney.
- That is correct.

725
00:45:22,053 --> 00:45:23,930
How about their first 200-yard rusher?

726
00:45:24,847 --> 00:45:27,599
- Frank Solich?
- First Heisman winner?

727
00:45:27,600 --> 00:45:29,393
- Johnny Rodgers.
- That's it.

728
00:45:30,186 --> 00:45:31,646
Where did Harry Potter go to school?

729
00:45:32,605 --> 00:45:33,606
Excuse me?

730
00:45:34,232 --> 00:45:37,109
Harry Potter, boy wizard.
What was the name of the school?

731
00:45:39,028 --> 00:45:40,029
I don't know.

732
00:45:41,322 --> 00:45:42,448
It was a book.

733
00:45:43,199 --> 00:45:44,282
I don't read a lot.

734
00:45:44,283 --> 00:45:47,077
Well, you go to the movies, don't you?
They only made, like, 22 of them.

735
00:45:47,078 --> 00:45:49,037
Oh, I watch a lot of football.

736
00:45:49,038 --> 00:45:51,498
- That's the rub, isn't it?
- What?

737
00:45:51,499 --> 00:45:53,583
Pretending to be someone that you're not.

738
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:54,793
You learn all the specifics,

739
00:45:54,794 --> 00:45:57,004
but you don't learn
what everyone else knows.

740
00:45:58,881 --> 00:46:01,217
I don't-- I don't understand.
Who are you, exactly?

741
00:46:02,718 --> 00:46:04,220
Hal Jordan, Green Lantern.

742
00:46:05,596 --> 00:46:08,473
Charged by the Guardians of the Universe
to protect Sector 2814

743
00:46:08,474 --> 00:46:09,892
from all extra-planetary threats.

744
00:46:10,434 --> 00:46:13,020
And you, Waylon, are one of them.

745
00:46:14,313 --> 00:46:17,941
Good Christ, he really is
full of himself, isn't he?

746
00:46:17,942 --> 00:46:19,401
Can't be easy,

747
00:46:19,402 --> 00:46:21,945
having to learn
from someone you don't respect.

748
00:46:21,946 --> 00:46:23,072
I do respect him.

749
00:46:23,614 --> 00:46:25,157
- Come on.
- I do.

750
00:46:25,658 --> 00:46:26,742
Why?

751
00:46:28,911 --> 00:46:30,578
I don't know. He's fearless.

752
00:46:30,579 --> 00:46:32,707
If you care about people,

753
00:46:33,249 --> 00:46:35,960
you know, husband, wife, parent, kid,

754
00:46:36,544 --> 00:46:38,212
then you're scared of losing them.

755
00:46:38,754 --> 00:46:40,380
First time he strutted up to me,

756
00:46:40,381 --> 00:46:43,634
I could tell Jordan doesn't
care about anybody.

757
00:46:44,260 --> 00:46:46,053
And nobody cares about him.

758
00:46:46,637 --> 00:46:48,306
He's not fucking fearless.

759
00:46:48,931 --> 00:46:49,932
He's lonely.

760
00:46:50,558 --> 00:46:52,350
<i>But why did you stick around?</i>

761
00:46:52,351 --> 00:46:53,852
What were you looking for?

762
00:46:53,853 --> 00:46:57,022
I mean, I get once I showed up,
you couldn't run. You had to blend in.

763
00:46:57,023 --> 00:46:58,273
But before that...

764
00:46:58,274 --> 00:47:00,608
I just went to a high school
football game, man.

765
00:47:00,609 --> 00:47:02,736
With the other Kimball fans
who are all dead now.

766
00:47:02,737 --> 00:47:06,114
I don't know them, okay?
I told you, I drive a truck.

767
00:47:06,115 --> 00:47:09,326
Yeah, I'm sure you can tell me a lot about
that truck, but I bet you can't tell me

768
00:47:09,327 --> 00:47:11,828
about the Boston Tea Party,
Kelly Clarkson,

769
00:47:11,829 --> 00:47:13,705
Barack Obama, or Rup--

770
00:47:13,706 --> 00:47:16,292
Barack Obama is the president
of the United States.

771
00:47:17,710 --> 00:47:18,711
That's it?

772
00:47:19,337 --> 00:47:21,504
As a rural Nebraskan, that's the breadth

773
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:23,966
of your opinion of Barack Hussein Obama?

774
00:47:27,470 --> 00:47:30,138
He is the 44th president.
He followed George W. Bush.

775
00:47:30,139 --> 00:47:33,100
There's some controversy
surrounding his birth certificate.

776
00:47:35,853 --> 00:47:38,564
Holy shit, you are an alien.

777
00:47:47,114 --> 00:47:48,449
Let's say you're right.

778
00:47:48,991 --> 00:47:49,992
Oh, fuck.

779
00:47:50,785 --> 00:47:52,744
<i>Let's say, hypothetically,</i>

780
00:47:52,745 --> 00:47:57,499
that I'm not of this salty, smelly world,
a visitor who went to great trouble

781
00:47:57,500 --> 00:48:00,085
to hide himself well
and learn the arcane rules

782
00:48:00,086 --> 00:48:03,671
of pointless contests involving balls
that somehow captivate more attention

783
00:48:03,672 --> 00:48:05,465
than the deteriorating atmosphere

784
00:48:05,466 --> 00:48:07,635
or the hunger
of its least fortunate people.

785
00:48:10,888 --> 00:48:12,639
If I had gone to such lengths,

786
00:48:12,640 --> 00:48:14,516
I would be here
for a very important purpose.

787
00:48:14,517 --> 00:48:17,143
A purpose that required
great discretion and secrecy.

788
00:48:17,144 --> 00:48:19,062
A purpose that would need
to be kept from the likes

789
00:48:19,063 --> 00:48:21,272
of a galactic peacekeeping organization

790
00:48:21,273 --> 00:48:23,859
because it concerns
the exact opposite of peace.

791
00:48:24,527 --> 00:48:25,611
That being war.

792
00:48:26,570 --> 00:48:27,862
And as such,

793
00:48:27,863 --> 00:48:30,615
if I were to fall into the hands
of such an organization,

794
00:48:30,616 --> 00:48:32,992
I would be forced to take drastic measures

795
00:48:32,993 --> 00:48:35,329
to ensure that my purpose
was not revealed.

796
00:48:37,998 --> 00:48:39,083
Hypothetically.

797
00:48:44,088 --> 00:48:47,590
And hypothetically, what might you have
to keep your mouth shut?

798
00:48:47,591 --> 00:48:50,009
- A cyanide pill?
- You're thinking very small.

799
00:48:50,010 --> 00:48:51,136
Then give it to me big.

800
00:48:51,137 --> 00:48:54,139
I'd have a biometric neutron device
woven into my skeleton.

801
00:48:54,140 --> 00:48:56,308
I'd be able to activate it with a thought.

802
00:48:57,768 --> 00:49:00,228
<i>Unless you let me walk out
that door right now.</i>

803
00:49:00,229 --> 00:49:02,021
He's bluffing, right?

804
00:49:02,022 --> 00:49:04,566
<i>You're not walking out
of here hypothetically or otherwise.</i>

805
00:49:04,567 --> 00:49:07,360
And if you do blow yourself up,
I'm just gonna bubble up

806
00:49:07,361 --> 00:49:09,529
and contain all that sunshine with my ring

807
00:49:09,530 --> 00:49:11,489
and walk out of here without a scratch.

808
00:49:11,490 --> 00:49:12,740
You've been here 48 hours.

809
00:49:12,741 --> 00:49:15,119
Did you bring the lantern
to recharge your ring?

810
00:49:16,912 --> 00:49:18,080
I have plenty of power.

811
00:49:20,082 --> 00:49:21,375
But for how much longer?

812
00:49:24,503 --> 00:49:25,504
Yeah.

813
00:49:31,010 --> 00:49:32,260
<i>You should be asking yourself</i>

814
00:49:32,261 --> 00:49:34,053
<i>if I'm capable of releasing enough energy</i>

815
00:49:34,054 --> 00:49:35,764
<i>to eradicate this entire town.</i>

816
00:49:37,808 --> 00:49:41,103
We talking or exploding?
Because it's almost lunchtime.

817
00:49:44,523 --> 00:49:46,442
It almost seems like you...

818
00:49:47,818 --> 00:49:52,281
want to die, Hal Jordan.
Does that not violate your precious oath?

819
00:49:53,365 --> 00:49:55,658
"In brightest day and blackest night..."

820
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:57,243
- Don't.
- "...no evil shall escape my sight."

821
00:49:57,244 --> 00:50:01,122
- Shut your mouth.
- "Let those who worship evil's might

822
00:50:01,123 --> 00:50:02,833
- beware my power...
- I said don't.

823
00:50:03,876 --> 00:50:05,753
"...Green Lantern's light."

824
00:50:09,131 --> 00:50:12,510
<i>Harry Potter went to Hogwarts,
you ignorant alien fuck!</i>

825
00:50:17,348 --> 00:50:19,807
- Are you beeping?
- Should we go? We should go.

826
00:50:19,808 --> 00:50:21,769
- No, it's too late.
<i>- Why are you here?</i>

827
00:50:22,603 --> 00:50:23,729
<i>Why else?</i>

828
00:50:24,396 --> 00:50:25,523
<i>Vengeance.</i>

829
00:50:59,640 --> 00:51:01,100
Told you he was an alien.

830
00:52:27,353 --> 00:52:30,438
Look at you. You've barely aged.

831
00:52:30,439 --> 00:52:31,482
Liar.

832
00:52:34,860 --> 00:52:35,986
How's Noah?

833
00:52:37,112 --> 00:52:39,782
Tall. He's on the team now.

834
00:52:40,282 --> 00:52:41,325
Quarterback.

835
00:52:42,409 --> 00:52:43,910
He any good?

836
00:52:43,911 --> 00:52:44,912
All-state.

837
00:52:47,498 --> 00:52:48,499
That's good.

838
00:52:53,420 --> 00:52:54,630
Anyone else know?

839
00:52:56,924 --> 00:52:58,425
Just the groundskeeper.

840
00:53:00,678 --> 00:53:01,679
All right.
